[32m+[m[32m# LabLink — Making College Laboratories More Accessible[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m> A GenAI-powered campus laboratory resource-sharing platform engineered to optimize instrument utilisation, streamline access workflows, and eliminate equipment conflicts across academic departments.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 1. Problem Statement[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mCollege laboratories frequently suffer from severe asymmetric utilisation:[m
[32m+[m[32m- High-end research instrumentation (e.g., GPU clusters, 3D printers, spectrophotometers, digital oscilloscopes) sits underutilized in one academic department while students and faculty in neighboring departments face scheduling deadlocks.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Traditional laboratory access relies on manual gatekeeping or naive First-Come-First-Served (FCFS) slot reservation, leading to booking monopolization, missed project deadlines, and inefficient resource allocation.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Students lack visibility into equipment availability across departments, struggle to map project technical requirements to suitable lab hardware, and face opaque eligibility barriers.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**LabLink** solves these systemic challenges through an accessible, high-contrast, unified web application featuring:[m
[32m+[m[32m1. Cross-departmental equipment discovery with transparent plain-language access policies.[m
[32m+[m[32m2. Conflict-free 1-hour slot scheduling with server-side clash detection and capacity tracking.[m
[32m+[m[32m3. Multi-constraint algorithmic fairness engine for slot contention resolution and batch allocation.[m
[32m+[m[32m4. GenAI project analysis, catalogue recommendation, application draft generation, and factual decision explanation with instant deterministic fallbacks.[m
[32m+[m[32m5. Administrative capacity analytics and empirical policy simulation comparing naive FCFS against optimized scheduling.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 2. Solution Overview[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mLabLink combines a **deterministic algorithmic core for fairness** with **Gemini AI for natural language understanding and explanation**. This architectural separation ensures the platform is fully verifiable, immune to hallucination, and operational even when offline or when external AI calls fail.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Key Highlights[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Single Deployable Service**: Node.js + Express backend serving both the RESTful `/api` endpoints and the compiled React SPA bundle.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Minimal Dependencies**: Zero heavy UI frameworks; built with pure accessible CSS, system fonts, and semantic HTML adhering to WCAG 2.1 AA standards.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Hardened Security**: Multi-layer input validation and sanitization, Helmet with strict Content-Security-Policy (CSP), dual-tiered rate limiting (stricter on GenAI routes), and prompt injection isolation.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Cloud Run Ready**: Containerized via a multi-stage Dockerfile (`node:20-alpine`), running as a non-root user, listening on `0.0.0.0:${PORT:-8080}` with response compression and immutable asset caching.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Zero Fabricated Metrics**: Every metric, percentage, score, and wait time rendered in the UI is computed dynamically from empirical data.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
